  "disposition_rationale": "The batch protocol relies on microwave irradiation, which provides rapid, volumetric heating and potentially specific non-thermal effects or superheating capabilities not directly replicable by standard convective heating in flow. While the temperature is low (50 C), the short residence time (10 min) and high yield suggest a fast reaction. Translating this to flow requires validating that convective heating at 50 C achieves the same conversion within the calculated residence time. The inventory supports the design (PFA coils, syringe pumps), but the lack of explicit mixing hardware and the change in heating method necessitate a screening approach to confirm kinetics and mixing efficiency before scale-up.",
